# Personal Codex overlay

This short file is the owner-private, Codex-specific entry point for this
personal layer. It is selected only by an explicit local
`setup-codex.sh --personal-layer <this-layer>` invocation, which builds an
untracked layer-4 global-instruction composite. Do not copy its contents into a
shared project or public repository.

## Personal-source routing

When a task requires owner-specific preferences, identity, account handling,
cross-repository state, or a personal operational rule, locate this personal
layer from the generated global-instruction header. Read its `CLAUDE.md` as
the private index, then open only the relevant linked source; do not preload a
large personal corpus into every task.

Keep durable private rules in their owning personal-layer files and current
work state in the relevant repository's `SESSION.md`. Keep the overlay short:
it should route Codex to the private source of truth, not duplicate it.
